hdw4s (2.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A desktop no longer stays blank when the browser declines the microphone
    or the camera.
  * Sessions use the GPU when the machine has one, which roughly halves what a
    desktop costs to stream.
  * The frame rate can be raised to 60 from the video settings panel.

 -- Markus Gutschke <gutschke@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:19:54 -0700

hdw4s (2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Retargeted to Selkies 2.0. A machine running the older Selkies needs the
    selkies-1.6 branch instead.
  * The microphone and the camera can be turned on, with HDW4S_MICROPHONE and
    HDW4S_WEBCAM. Both are off by default.
  * sudo works from a desktop, governed by sudoers as it is anywhere else.
  * An account gets one desktop per machine.
  * A second browser takes a desktop over without asking first, where 1.1
    offered a button. Reloading the first window takes it back.

 -- Markus Gutschke <gutschke@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:29:37 -0700

hdw4s (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A desktop can now be moved between devices. It belongs to one browser at a
    time; a second is told it is open elsewhere and offered a button to take it
    over, and the device that had it is told so and offered the same way back.
    A reload or a dropped connection is recognised as the same window returning
    rather than as a second device.
  * Turning a second client away no longer writes a traceback per attempt. A
    client that could not recognise the refusal reconnected several times a
    second; one stuck browser logged 17858 of them in two days.
  * A closed signalling socket can no longer stop a session. The desktop's read
    loop ran its callbacks inline and they sent on the same socket, so a close
    arriving mid-callback escaped into a bare exception handler and exited the
    process -- taking the desktop and every window open in it.
  * The updater checks what it downloaded against a recorded checksum, and says
    so plainly when it has nothing to check a hand-pinned version against.
  * The idle reaper counts the clients attached to a session rather than the
    session's own connections, so a desktop in use is no longer stopped.
  * "hdw4s show" reports whether session hand-over is in effect, which of its
    two halves is present, and the close codes a browser is turned away with.
  * "hdw4s list" and "hdw4s show" no longer report an authenticated session as
    unprotected when the caller cannot read its credential.

 -- Markus Gutschke <gutschke@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700

